{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/77","id":4957082187,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUJ8YLs8AAAABJ3cSSw","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/pull/77","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/pull/77.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/pull/77.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/issues/77","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/77/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/77/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/issues/77/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/packages/statuses/94d63a3c099dcaa69bcefda3b021bafcc8d828f6","number":77,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"test: verify native preview and diagnose installed client phases","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?[query-redacted]","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Composite delivery preparation previously used a structural preview fixture, leaving its preview signatures and native archive outside the exercised chain. This adds a real TEST ONLY preview export alongside two stable generations and runs the native verifiers, canonical archive/audit checks, composite planner and materializer across 29 cases. The data-only export reuses signing/candidate helpers while the original client export retains its real-binary and fixed-source checks. Test secrets are removed before independent verification; production fresh-input verification rejects synthetic provenance.\n\nThe existing native safety workflow gains an isolated fixture step and public JSON receipts. Its original candidate and 49-client gates remain. Installed-client commands now emit fixed phase markers around checksum, RPM signature, dependency installation and CLI acceptance. A bounded diagnostic summary preserves early markers even when the output tail no longer contains them. These observations do not decide acceptance; the commands, images, resources, 600/650-second limits, cleanup and receipt validation are unchanged.\n\nValidation: tests were written first. The new native fixture passed all 29 cases locally and on the first Linux CI at 19ce29fb; the old native repository drills, 572 default tests and SDK 22+10 checks also passed there. The original 49-client gate failed its first Alma installation after 600.151 seconds (exit 124): zero cases passed, one failed, 48 were not reached. Checksum and RPM signature passed, but the old output cannot distinguish dependency work from redirected CLI acceptance. That failure is preserved; it was not retried.\n\nThe diagnostic increment at 94d63a3c passed nine new process tests after their first red, the full local default suite (580 passed and one existing RPM environment skip), four contracts, and independent Standards/Spec review with zero findings. Independent probes also verified command equivalence and phase retention after more than 4096 bytes of output. Its first exact-head Linux CI is pending. The historical Alma timeout cause remains unknown; no completed 49-client gate is claimed.\n\nThe fixture's earlier PID exhaustion was separately reproduced and repaired by using init only for the new container, with unchanged resource limits and assertions. That failure is retained in the evidence. These are preparation and diagnostics: stable stays disabled, and this PR does not claim live CDN, production provenance, public-client acceptance or publication.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T19:20:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T20:10:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1625487a0ffc18090047dcfce65113a62595b1de","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/native-preview-fixture","ref":"codex/native-preview-fixture","repo":{"id":1352603694,"node_id":"R_kgDOUJ8YLg","name":"packages","full_name":"WuKongIM/packages","owner":{"login":"WuKongIM","id":132860831,"node_id":"O_kgDOB-tLnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132860831?[query-redacted]","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Signe